<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elwell Otis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1838">1838</a>–<a href="/years/1909">1909</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Elwell Stephen Otis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elwell Otis was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army general who served as military governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1898 to 1900. He commanded American forces at the outbreak of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a> in 1899 and repeatedly claimed the insurgency was nearly over. He was succeeded by Arthur MacArthur in 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elwell-otis.jpg" alt="Elwell Otis" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kurz &amp; Allison · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elwell_S._Otis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
